% ============================================================================
% frog-life-cycle.query.adj — worked recall over the frog life-cycle
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what position is this
% stage in the life cycle?" (direct) or "which stage comes first/second/
% etc.?" (reverse) — it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries.
% ============================================================================

import "frog-life-cycle.adj"

? frog_life_stage(tadpole, $N)   % expect 2 (direct: what position is the tadpole stage?)
? frog_life_stage($S, 1)         % expect egg (reverse: which stage comes first?)
? frog_life_stage(adult, $N)     % expect abstain -- "adult" is not one of the three tabled stage names
